{
  "scope": "Read-only review of shared power policy and both platform integration paths. This review adds no executable qualification and makes no target scheduler/RF/power claim. Parent-owned host/SDK checks are independent.",
  "review_utc": "2026-10-19T14:42:19.090926+00:00",
  "actionable_findings": [],
  "observations": [
    "Only accepted audio control commands establish a new generation; receive/finish use exact equality. Unsigned wrap does not rely on ordering comparisons.",
    "Command hooks do not allocate, call Wi-Fi or wait. Policy copies use one short portMUX region; the SDK callback runs outside it. Existing task core bindings remain untouched.",
    "Stale successful driver calls update applied mode while preserving the latest desired retry budget; the next poll reconciles newer intent. Driver lifetime revision invalidates an older callback result.",
    "Each desired revision has at most three failed attempts separated by at least 250 ms; int64 deadline saturation is explicit. A known correct applied mode does not issue another call.",
    "CYD owner_step is the sole CYD poll caller after started. C3 permanent RSSI task is the sole C3 poll caller, every 100 ms, with RSSI retaining its 2-second cadence and sleep admission guard.",
    "Wi-Fi power SDK errors remain independent of Play admission. EOF restores idle intent when receive ends, allowing buffered PCM to drain as the donor contract states.",
    "C3 prepare_sleep guard cannot cancel an already entered driver call; SDK stop/set_ps serialization remains an SDK boundary. No new driver lifetime teardown is added and this is not a reproduced defect."
  ],
